    "body": "## Problem\n\n`update_last_checkpoint_symlink()` in `swift/utils/io_utils.py` uses a fixed staging path (`last-checkpoint.tmp`) for every update. Concurrent checkpoint-save callbacks can interfere with each other's temporary symlinks, so one caller can report success while publishing another caller's checkpoint target.\n\n## Fix\n\nGive each update a unique temporary name (`<link>.<uuid4>.tmp`) before the atomic `os.replace`, so concurrent writers no longer share a staging path.\n\n## Test\n\nAdded `test_last_checkpoint_symlink_under_concurrency` to `tests/utils/test_io_utils.py`, exercising concurrent updates and asserting no leftover `.tmp` files.\n\nFixes #10336",
    "changed_files": 2,
    "closed_at": "2026-10-16T10:29:37Z",
